SOAPBOX: This year I decided to participate in CQ WW SSB on the 10m, SO(A) HP. On Saturday the propagation went smoothly, with favorable connections to Asia, the Far East, and in the afternoon to North America. Sunday saw much altered propagation compared to the previous day. There were short openings to VK only a few JAs stations were heard. In the afternoon, all North American stations were absent, with South American stations being numerous. Given my unfavorable geographic location (extremely hilly terrain with a small hill obstructing the southeast), I was able to log over 30 SA stations. The final list lacked zones 1, 3, 29, and 31. I operate the IC-730Mk2, Acom 2000A, and OB16-3. Thanks to everyone for the QSOs and for being patient. CU on the CW stage.
